      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "Hm - we have not been able to reproduce this issue. I personally use git for all of my VRChat Avatar and World projects, and I'm able to add them to the Creator Companion just fine.\nHere's the logic for how we determine a project's type:\nFirst we look at the project's manifest in Packages/manifest.json.\nIf it has the Worlds package in it, it's a Worlds project.\nElse if it has the Avatars package in it, it's an Avatars project.\nElse if it has the Base package in it, it's a Starter project.\nElse if it has no Assets folder, it's an Unknown project.\nElse if it has an Assets/Udon folder, it's a Legacy SDK3 Worlds project.\nElse if it doesn't have an Assets/VRCSDK/Plugins folder, it's an Unknown project.\nElse if the above plugins folder has a file named \"VRCSDK3A.dll\", it's a Legacy Avatars project.\nElse if the above plugins folder has a file named \"VRCSDK2.dll\", it's a Legacy SDK2 project.\nElse it's an Unknown project.\nUsing the logic above, hopefully you can figure out why this project is appearing to be an \"Unknown\" proejct. If you've got a valid setup that doesn't match the rule above, let us know so we can adjust them!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
